// Declarative Net Request semantics, one row per case Chrome documents or
// Chromium tests. Each row's source names where its expectation comes from
// ('chromium:<file> <test>', 'docs:<section of developer.chrome.com's
// declarativeNetRequest reference>', or 'native'); every native row was
// checked against Chrome 157 (testMatchOutcome, isRegexSupported, rule
// updates and unpacked loads), and a row whose source Chrome disagreed with
// carries the source's expectation in its note.
//
// Row shapes:
//   urlFilterCases: { name, source, urlFilter, isUrlFilterCaseSensitive?, url, expect }
//   validationCases: { name, source, rule, rulesetKind, expectError, message?,
//     expectWarning?, count?, rulesetCount?, enabledRulesetCount? }: count is
//     how many copies of rule (ids 1..count) the ruleset holds, rulesetCount
//     how many static rulesets the manifest declares (each holding them) and
//     enabledRulesetCount how many of those are enabled. expectError is a
//     ParseResult name, or 'api:<constant>' / 'manifest:<constant>' for the
//     limits Chrome checks outside rule parsing. expectWarning marks a rule
//     Chrome skips with a warning instead of failing the load.
//   regexCases: { name, source, regex, isCaseSensitive?, requireCapturing?, expect }
//   matchCases: { name, source, rules | extensions, request, frames?, expect, native }

